# Lumenhold Academy — 简体中文 (zh-CN) translation of content/events/pools/dating.grim
# Maintained by `node tools/grim.js i18n zh-CN`. Translate the text after "="; keep {tokens}.
# "# en:" shows the English source. [hash] marks the English version a line was translated from;
# lines marked STALE need updating — after fixing the text, delete the [hash] and re-run the tool.


@event date_market_day
# en: Market Day
title [0bcdaf] = 集市日
# en: {Market day in the village, and {partner} has decided you're going together.|Market day again. {partner} knows which stall has the good pies now.|{partner} has a list for the market, and you're on it.} {~A stall sells hats nobody should wear.|There's a juggler with one ball too many.|{season == "winter": Roasted chestnuts, paper cones, cold fingers.|Strawberries, a whole cart of them.}}
text [c6d33f] = {村里的集市日，{partner} 已经决定你们要一起去。|又是集市日。{partner} 现在知道哪个摊子的派好吃了。|{partner} 列了一张集市清单，你也在上面。} {~有个摊子卖谁都不该戴的帽子。|有个杂耍艺人多抛了一个球。|{season == "winter": 烤栗子、纸筒、冻僵的手指。|草莓，整整一车。}}
# en: Two students wandering a village market arm in arm, stalls of ribbons and pies, one holding up a ridiculous hat.
scene [08939c] = 两个学生挽着胳膊逛村里的集市，摊位上挂着丝带、摆着馅饼，其中一个举起一顶滑稽的帽子。
# en: Buy {them} something silly
opt.left.label [89db94] = 给 {them} 买点傻东西
# en: {~You buy {partner} the worst hat at the market. {They} wear{s} it all day, with enormous dignity.|A tin ring from a pedlar, too big for any finger. {partner} threads it on a string and doesn't take it off.}
opt.left.say.1 [39cf17] = {~你给 {partner} 买了集市上最丑的帽子。{They} 戴了一整天，极其庄重。|从小贩那儿买来一枚锡戒指，哪根手指戴都太大。{partner} 把它穿在绳子上，再没摘下来。}
# en: Just walk and talk
opt.right.label [a304f1] = 就走走聊聊
# en: {~You walk the whole market twice and buy nothing but a pie to share. You talk the entire time and remember none of it, only the voice.|An afternoon of nothing in particular, which is exactly what you both needed.}
opt.right.say.1 [d33689] = {~你们把整个集市逛了两遍，除了一个分着吃的馅饼什么都没买。你们一直在聊，聊了什么一句也不记得，只记得那个声音。|一个无所事事的下午，正是你们俩都需要的。}

@event date_study_together
# en: Studying Together
title [1131fc] = 一起学习
# en: {{partner} suggests studying together. In theory, this is efficient.|Another study evening with {partner}. The theory remains a theory.|{partner} has saved you a seat in the library and stacked your books for you.} {~The exam is in a fortnight.|The library is very quiet.|Your knees keep touching under the table.}
text [00d6e4] = {{partner} 提议一起学习。理论上，这很高效。|又一个和 {partner} 一起学习的晚上。理论依然只是理论。|{partner} 在图书馆给你占了座，还把你的书摞好了。} {~考试还有两个星期。|图书馆非常安静。|你们的膝盖在桌子底下一直碰到一起。}
# en: Two students at a library table, books piled between them, one pretending to read while watching the other.
scene [10169c] = 图书馆的桌旁，两个学生之间堆着书，一个假装在读，其实在看另一个。
# en: Actually study
opt.left.label [c324b5] = 认真学习
# en: {~You study, properly, in companionable silence. {partner} sighs once, theatrically. You both pass the next quiz.|Two hours of real work. {partner} quizzes you on the walk back, and you get them all right.}
opt.left.say.1 [c9d807] = {~你们在惬意的沉默中好好学习。{partner} 夸张地叹了一次气。你们俩下次小测都过了。|两个小时实打实的功课。回去的路上 {partner} 考你，你全答对了。}
# en: Don't study at all
opt.right.label [82fa8a] = 完全不学
# en: {~You pass notes, then drawings, then you're both thrown out of the library for laughing. Worth it.|Not a page is turned. The librarian moves you apart, which only makes it worse.}
opt.right.say.1 [c9c7ef] = {~你们传纸条，然后传画，然后因为笑得太大声被一起赶出了图书馆。值了。|一页书都没翻。图书管理员把你们分开坐，结果更糟了。}

@event date_first_quarrel
# en: A Quarrel
title [719a6c] = 一次争吵
# en: Your first real quarrel with {partner}. It started about something small, a missed supper, and became about something large before either of you noticed. Now you're on opposite ends of a bench and neither of you will speak first.
text [14e59c] = 你和 {partner} 第一次真正的争吵。起因是件小事，一顿错过的晚饭，在两人都没察觉的时候，变成了一件大事。现在你们各坐长椅一头，谁也不肯先开口。
# en: Two students on opposite ends of a cold courtyard bench, not looking at each other, a dropped scarf between them.
scene [ebd0c4] = 两个学生坐在冷清庭院里一张长椅的两端，互不相看，中间掉着一条围巾。
# en: Speak first
opt.left.label [e3b9df] = 先开口
# en: "I'm sorry," you say, and it costs you. {partner} looks at you, then shuffles along the bench. "Me too." You talk it through until the bell. It's better after, and you both know how it's done now.
opt.left.say.1 [9514e8] = “对不起，”你说，说出这句话不容易。{partner} 看着你，然后挪了过来。“我也是。”你们一直谈到钟响。之后好多了，你们俩也都知道该怎么和好了。
# en: Wait for {them}
opt.right.label [bbb6ab] = 等 {them} 先开口
# en: You wait. So does {partner}. You leave separately. The next day you both pretend it didn't happen, and it lies between you like the scarf on the bench.
opt.right.say.1 [efe5a6] = 你等着。{partner} 也等着。你们各自离开。第二天你们都假装什么也没发生，它横在你们之间，就像长椅上那条围巾。

@event date_meet_friends
# en: Meeting the Friends
title [92ece0] = 见朋友
# en: {friend} and {partner} have heard a great deal about each other, all from you, and now they're at the same supper table. {friend} is being very polite. {partner} is being very polite back. You are dying.
text [91a7b1] = {friend} 和 {partner} 从你嘴里听说了对方很多事，现在他们坐在同一张晚餐桌旁。{friend} 非常有礼貌。{partner} 也非常有礼貌地回应。你快死了。
# en: Three students around a refectory table, two of them sizing each other up over the bread basket, one in the middle smiling too hard.
scene [1fa419] = 膳堂桌旁的三个学生，其中两个隔着面包篮互相打量，夹在中间的那个笑得太用力。
# en: Steer the talk to something they share
opt.left.label [6a05ef] = 把话题引向他们的共同点
# en: You find it on the third try: a shared loathing of Thursday's soup. By pudding they're ganging up on you, which is exactly what you wanted.
opt.left.say.1 [988245] = 试到第三次你找到了：两人都痛恨星期四的汤。到吃甜点时，他们已经联手对付你了，这正是你想要的。
# en: Every subject dies. They're kind about it, both of them, and the silence is very long. "Well," says {friend}, afterwards. "They're nice." It's not quite a compliment.
opt.left.say.2 [055ea9] = 每个话题都冷了场。他们俩对此都很客气，沉默非常漫长。“嗯，”事后 {friend} 说，“人挺好的。”这不完全是夸奖。
# en: Let them find their own way
opt.right.label [a54eb8] = 让他们自己找到相处之道
# en: You eat your supper and let them circle each other. By the end they've agreed on nothing except that you talk in your sleep. You never find out how {partner} knew that and {friend} did.
opt.right.say.1 [bde158] = 你吃着晚饭，让他们互相试探。到最后，他们除了一致认为你说梦话之外，什么都没达成共识。你始终没弄明白 {partner} 和 {friend} 是怎么知道的。

@event date_rainy_afternoon
# en: Rained In
title [95b599] = 被雨困住
# en: {Rain all afternoon, and {partner} has found the window seat in the west tower, a blanket and an old board game with half the pieces.|Rain again. The window seat is yours now, by custom.|{partner} has brought new pieces for the game, carved from soap.} {~The rain is loud on the leads.|The tea is too hot.|The game's rules are mostly invented.}
text [f1c11a] = {下了一下午的雨，{partner} 找到了西塔的窗边座位、一条毯子和一副缺了一半棋子的旧棋盘游戏。|又下雨了。按惯例，窗边座位现在归你们了。|{partner} 带来了新棋子，是用肥皂刻的。} {~雨打在铅皮屋顶上很响。|茶太烫了。|游戏规则大多是编的。}
# en: Rain streaming down a tall window seat, two students under one blanket with a board game between them, cups of tea steaming.
scene [ce0ce8] = 雨水顺着高高的窗户淌下，窗边座位上两个学生裹着一条毯子，中间摆着棋盘，茶杯冒着热气。
# en: Play to win
opt.left.label [6c2256] = 认真求胜
# en: {~You win, ruthlessly. {partner} demands a rematch and wins that. Neither of you will ever forget the score.|You cheat; {partner} cheats better. The game ends in a pillow fight and a broken teacup.}
opt.left.say.1 [a0a32e] = {~你赢了，毫不留情。{partner} 要求再来一局，然后赢了。你们俩永远都不会忘记这个比分。|你作弊；{partner} 作弊作得更好。游戏以一场枕头大战和一只摔碎的茶杯告终。}
# en: Forget the game
opt.right.label [13db77] = 忘了游戏
# en: {~The game is abandoned by the second move. You talk about your families until the rain stops and the room is dark and you're late for supper.|You fall asleep under the blanket and wake up cold and late and very happy.}
opt.right.say.1 [58e8bb] = {~第二步游戏就被抛在了一边。你们聊着各自的家人，直到雨停，屋里黑了，晚饭也迟到了。|你们在毯子底下睡着了，醒来时又冷又晚，非常快乐。}

@event date_forgotten_day
# en: The Day You Forgot
title [58f7f4] = 你忘了的日子
# en: {partner} hands you a small parcel, wrapped carefully, and says "Happy half-year." You didn't know there was a half-year. You have nothing. {partner} sees you realise it.
text [bade45] = {partner} 递给你一个小包裹，包得很仔细，说：“半周年快乐。”你都不知道还有半周年。你什么也没准备。{partner} 看见你反应过来了。
# en: A student holding a small wrapped present out to another student, whose hands are empty and whose face has just fallen.
scene [cac280] = 一个学生把一个小小的包好的礼物递向另一个学生，对方两手空空，脸刚刚垮下来。
# en: Confess and make it up
opt.left.label [112bdb] = 坦白，然后补救
# en: "I forgot," you say. {They} laugh{s}, a little hurt. That evening you turn up with flowers from the village and a terrible poem, and the poem does it.
opt.left.say.1 [d71455] = “我忘了，”你说。{They} 笑了，有一点受伤。那天晚上你带着从村里买来的花和一首糟糕的诗出现，是那首诗打动了 {them}。
# en: Pretend your gift is "coming"
opt.right.label [d78c81] = 假装你的礼物“在路上”
# en: You run to the village before the shops shut and spend more than you meant on something you hope looks planned. {partner} believes you, or kindly pretends to.
opt.right.say.1 [f03c99] = 你赶在商店关门前跑到村里，花了比预想更多的钱，买了一件希望看起来像是早有准备的东西。{partner} 相信了你，或者好心地装作相信。
# en: The shops are shut. Your gift "is delayed" for a week. {partner} doesn't ask about it again, and that is worse than asking.
opt.right.say.2 [bd2585] = 商店都关门了。你的礼物“延误了”一个星期。{partner} 再也没问起过，这比问起更糟。

@event date_dance_lesson
# en: Learning to Dance
title [2d93c7] = 学跳舞
# en: {With the {month == 4: Midwinter Ball|Starfall dance} coming, {partner} has decided you're going to learn properly, in an empty classroom, with the chairs pushed back.|Another lesson. You're on the second dance now, which has a spin.|"Again," says {partner}. "From the turn."} {~Somebody is watching from the door.|Your feet have opinions.|There's no music, only counting.}
text [c2670d] = {{month == 4: 仲冬舞会|星坠节舞会}快到了，{partner} 决定要你好好学一学，在一间空教室里，椅子都推到了墙边。|又一堂课。你们已经学到第二支舞了，有个转圈。|“再来，”{partner} 说。“从转身开始。”} {~有人在门口偷看。|你的脚自有主张。|没有音乐，只有数拍子。}
# en: Two students practising dance steps in an empty classroom, chairs pushed back, one counting aloud and the other looking at their feet.
scene [ba646d] = 空教室里两个学生在练舞步，椅子推到一边，一个大声数着拍子，另一个盯着自己的脚。
# en: Practise until it's right
opt.left.label [efeeed] = 练到对为止
# en: {~By the end of the hour you can do the turn without looking. {partner} says "There," very softly, and doesn't let go straight away.|Your feet ache, and you can dance. Nearly.}
opt.left.say.1 [ab48d0] = {~一个小时结束时，你已经能不看脚就转身了。{partner} 很轻地说了声“对了”，没有马上松手。|你的脚很疼，但你会跳舞了。差不多吧。}
# en: Make it a joke
opt.right.label [9667e2] = 当成玩笑
# en: {~You invent a new dance, mostly flailing. {partner} laughs so hard {they} ha{s} to sit down, then joins in.|You never learn the turn. You learn that {partner} snorts when {they} laugh{s}, which is better.}
opt.right.say.1 [be290c] = {~你发明了一种新舞，主要是乱扑腾。{partner} 笑得不得不坐下来，然后也加入了。|你始终没学会那个转身。你学到的是 {partner} 笑起来会打鼻响，这更好。}

@event date_after_graduation
# en: After
title [dd3a69] = 以后
# en: On the castle wall at sunset, {partner} asks the question neither of you has said out loud: "After graduation. What happens to us?" The valley below is gold. {They} {are} not looking at you, very deliberately.
text [f84ba7] = 日落时分的城墙上，{partner} 问出了你们俩都没说出口的那个问题：“毕业以后。我们怎么办？”下面的山谷一片金黄。{They} 很刻意地没有看你。
# en: Two students sitting on the castle wall at sunset, legs dangling, the whole valley below them gold.
scene [b579db] = 日落时分，两个学生坐在城墙上，双腿悬空，下方整个山谷一片金黄。
# en: "We go together."
opt.left.label [1a21cd] = “我们一起走。”
# en: {They} let{s} out a breath {they}'d been holding for months. You plan it there and then, badly: a city, a cottage, a list of rules for the kitchen. It doesn't matter that it's badly. It's yours.
opt.left.say.1 [0e5dc5] = {They} 长长地呼出一口憋了好几个月的气。你们当场就规划起来，规划得很糟：一座城市，一间小屋，一张厨房规矩清单。规划得糟不要紧。那是你们的。
# en: "Let's not decide yet."
opt.right.label [7da709] = “先别决定。”
# en: "Not yet," {they} agree{s}, too quickly, and takes your hand. You watch the gold go grey. It's honest, and it's lonelier than the other answer.
opt.right.say.1 [726a88] = “先不急，”{they} 答应得太快，然后握住了你的手。你们看着金色褪成灰色。这很诚实，也比另一个答案更孤单。

@event lyra_date_dawn_duel
# en: A Duel at Dawn
title [238c77] = 黎明决斗
# en: {Lyra's idea of a romantic morning is a duel at dawn in the empty courtyard, "to keep you sharp".|Another dawn duel. Lyra has started calling them "our mornings".|Lyra is already in the courtyard, wand out, mist on her shoulders.} {~She's brought coffee for after.|She's in a terrible mood, which means she slept well.|"No holding back," she says. "I'll know."}
text [303a4f] = {莱拉心目中浪漫的早晨，是在空荡的庭院里来一场黎明决斗，“让你保持敏锐”。|又一场黎明决斗。莱拉开始管它们叫“我们的早晨”了。|莱拉已经在庭院里了，魔杖在手，肩上落着雾。} {~她带了咖啡，留着决斗后喝。|她心情糟透了，这说明她睡得很好。|“不许留手，”她说。“我会知道的。”}
# en: Two duellists bowing in a misty courtyard at dawn, wands lowered, both trying not to smile.
scene [faa89f] = 雾气弥漫的黎明庭院里，两名决斗者垂下魔杖互相鞠躬，都在努力憋着不笑。
# en: Duel her properly
opt.left.label [356d49] = 认真和她决斗
# en: {~You win. Lyra stares at you as if you'd proposed. "Again," she says, breathless, and then, "Tomorrow." It's the best thing anyone has ever said to you.|A clean win. She shakes your hand, then doesn't let go of it.}
opt.left.say.1 [895d35] = {~你赢了。莱拉盯着你，好像你刚向她求了婚。“再来，”她喘着气说，然后，“明天。”这是有人对你说过的最好的话。|一场干净利落的胜利。她和你握手，然后没有松开。}
# en: {~She wins, because she always does, and then sits beside you on the cold steps with the coffee and explains your mistake, very gently, for her.|You lose. She bandages your knuckle herself and pretends it's an inspection.}
opt.left.say.2 [a7ddfd] = {~她赢了，因为她总是赢，然后和你一起坐在冰冷的台阶上喝咖啡，讲解你的失误，以她的标准来说非常温柔。|你输了。她亲手给你包扎指关节，假装这是一次检查。}
# en: Let her win, and tell her so
opt.right.label [6e593e] = 让她赢，并告诉她
# en: {~She knows the moment you drop your guard. "Don't you dare," she says, and then kisses you, furious, and then makes you do it again properly.|She's outraged. She's also, for the rest of the day, unusually soft.}
opt.right.say.1 [c6e076] = {~你一放下防守，她就知道了。“你敢，”她说，然后吻了你，气冲冲的，然后逼你好好再打一遍。|她气坏了。可她这一整天也格外温柔。}

@event tobias_date_greenhouse_supper
# en: Supper Among the Tomatoes
title [13d785] = 番茄丛中的晚餐
# en: {Tobias has cooked supper in the greenhouse, at a table between the tomato rows, with everything he grew himself.|Supper in the greenhouse again. The tomatoes have names now.|Tobias has added a second candle and a jar of wildflowers.} {~The soup is his grandmother's recipe.|A tomato plant is leaning in to listen.|There is far too much bread.}
text [605018] = {托比亚斯在温室里做了晚饭，桌子摆在番茄垄之间，所有东西都是他亲手种的。|又是温室里的晚餐。番茄们现在都有名字了。|托比亚斯多点了一根蜡烛，还摆了一罐野花。} {~汤是他祖母的配方。|一株番茄凑过来偷听。|面包多得离谱。}
# en: A candlelit table set up between rows of tomato plants in a warm greenhouse at night, a big student serving soup from a pot.
scene [128ebb] = 夜里温暖的温室中，番茄垄之间摆着一张烛光餐桌，一个大个子学生正从锅里盛汤。
# en: Eat everything, and ask for seconds
opt.left.label [0c79a4] = 全吃光，再要一份
# en: {~You eat three bowls and he beams like the sun. He tells you about the farm, the goats, the year the river froze. You could listen for ever, and nearly do.|Seconds, thirds, a slice of pie. Tobias watches you eat with an expression you want to keep in a jar.}
opt.left.say.1 [799b78] = {~你吃了三碗，他笑得像太阳。他给你讲农场、山羊、河水结冰的那一年。你可以一直听下去，也差点就这么做了。|第二份、第三份、一块派。托比亚斯看你吃饭的表情，你想装进罐子里留着。}
# en: Help him in the beds after
opt.right.label [b0cee6] = 饭后帮他打理苗床
# en: {~You weed the beds by lantern light, side by side. Your back aches; your hands smell of tomato leaves. He hums the whole time.|An hour of planting. He shows you how to tell a seedling it's doing well. You feel ridiculous, and do it anyway.}
opt.right.say.1 [63acb4] = {~你们借着灯笼光并肩除草。你的背很酸，手上满是番茄叶的气味。他一直哼着歌。|种了一个小时的苗。他教你怎么告诉一株幼苗它长得很好。你觉得自己很可笑，但还是照做了。}

@event seraphine_date_a_future
# en: A Future She Saw
title [d092d0] = 她看见的未来
# en: {Seraphine says she's seen a future with the two of you in it, and wants to tell you about it on the observatory floor, under the open dome.|Another future, another evening on the observatory floor.|"I saw us again," Seraphine says, lying down beside you. "Older."} {~She's shuffling the cards without looking.|The dome is full of stars.|She is, for once, entirely in the present.}
text [9a15b6] = {瑟拉芬说她看见了一个有你们俩的未来，想在观星台敞开的穹顶下、躺在地板上讲给你听。|又一个未来，又一个躺在观星台地板上的夜晚。|“我又看见我们了，”瑟拉芬在你身边躺下说。“老了以后。”} {~她看都不看地洗着牌。|穹顶里满是星星。|难得一次，她完完全全地活在当下。}
# en: A seer and a student lying on the observatory floor beneath the open dome, a scatter of tarot cards between them.
scene [1af1ef] = 一位预言者和一个学生躺在观星台敞开的穹顶下的地板上，两人之间散落着塔罗牌。
# en: Ask her to tell you
opt.left.label [fb782a] = 请她讲给你听
# en: {~She tells you: a kitchen, a cat, a terrible argument about curtains, a garden. It's so ordinary you could cry. She says it's her favourite one.|A future with snow in it, and a child who isn't yours or hers but stays anyway. She stops halfway and holds your hand.}
opt.left.say.1 [e3e29e] = {~她讲了：一间厨房，一只猫，一场关于窗帘的激烈争吵，一座花园。平凡得让你想哭。她说这是她最喜欢的一个。|一个下着雪的未来，还有一个既不是你的也不是她的孩子，却留了下来。她讲到一半停下，握住了你的手。}
# en: Ask her not to
opt.right.label [5b1e61] = 请她别讲
# en: {~"Let it surprise us," you say. She looks at you as if no one has ever asked her that. Then she puts the cards away, all of them.|She's quiet a while, then laughs. "You're the only person I can't read," she says. "It's very restful."}
opt.right.say.1 [408e69] = {~“让它给我们一个惊喜吧，”你说。她看着你，好像从来没有人这样要求过她。然后她把牌收了起来，全部。|她沉默了一会儿，然后笑了。“你是我唯一读不透的人，”她说。“这很让人放松。”}

@event corvin_date_rooftop_supper
# en: Supper on the Roof
title [5ad156] = 屋顶晚餐
# en: {Corvin leads you through three passages and a window to a rooftop between chimneys, where a tablecloth and supper are waiting.|Another rooftop, another tablecloth. You don't ask where he finds them.|"New roof," says Corvin. "Better view. Mostly legal."} {~The pastries are from the headmistress's own kitchen.|There's a candle in a jam jar.|He's brought cushions, which is unlike him.}
text [99290b] = {科尔文领你穿过三条通道和一扇窗户，来到烟囱之间的一片屋顶，那儿铺着桌布，晚餐已经备好了。|又一片屋顶，又一块桌布。你没问他从哪儿找来的。|“新屋顶，”科尔文说。“视野更好。基本合法。”} {~酥皮点心来自院长自己的厨房。|果酱罐里点着一根蜡烛。|他带了靠垫，这可不像他。}
# en: A tablecloth spread on a castle rooftop between chimneys, a candle in a jar, two students eating pastries above the sleeping towers.
scene [3fb767] = 城堡屋顶的烟囱之间铺着一块桌布，罐子里点着蜡烛，两个学生在沉睡的塔楼上方吃着酥皮点心。
# en: Ask where the supper came from
opt.left.label [7accc3] = 问晚餐是哪儿来的
# en: {~"Borrowed," he says. From the headmistress's kitchen. You eat it anyway, and it tastes of getting away with something. He grins all evening.|"Don't ask, saint." You don't. The pastries are perfect.}
opt.left.say.1 [2e0550] = {~“借的，”他说。从院长的厨房借的。你还是吃了，吃起来有一种逃过一劫的味道。他咧嘴笑了一整晚。|“别问，圣人。”你没问。点心完美无缺。}
# en: Just enjoy it
opt.right.label [a859b1] = 尽情享受
# en: {~You eat supper on the roof until the candle gutters. He doesn't make a single joke for a whole hour, and when you notice, he kisses you to stop you saying so.|The chimneys are warm, the air is cold, and you climb down at midnight scraped and happy.}
opt.right.say.1 [8e9ac8] = {~你们在屋顶上吃到蜡烛燃尽。整整一个小时他一个笑话都没讲，你注意到的时候，他吻了你，不让你说出来。|烟囱是暖的，空气是冷的，你们半夜爬下来，蹭破了皮，满心欢喜。}

@event mira_date_invention
# en: They Built You Something
title [bcced4] = TA 给你做了个东西
# en: {Mir has built you a present, a brass bird that sings your name, mostly.|Another present from Mir's bench, ticking ominously.|Mir presents their newest invention with a flourish and a fire bucket.} {~It's warm to the touch.|It has seven moving parts and one they don't explain.|"It's probably safe," they say.}
text [d5ac80] = {米尔给你做了一件礼物，一只会唱你名字的黄铜鸟，大致会唱。|米尔工作台上的又一件礼物，嘀嗒作响，不太妙。|米尔挥手一扬，展示 TA 的最新发明，旁边备着一只消防桶。} {~摸上去是温的。|它有七个活动部件，还有一个 TA 不肯解释。|“应该是安全的，”TA 说。}
# en: A cluttered workshop bench, a small brass contraption with wings sitting on it, a grinning inventor and a nervous student leaning away.
scene [3fca62] = 杂乱的工作台上放着一个带翅膀的小小黄铜装置，一个咧嘴笑的发明家，和一个紧张地往后仰的学生。
# en: Wind it up at once
opt.left.label [5a2193] = 马上上发条
# en: {~It sings your name, slightly wrong, all the way round the workshop, and lands in your hand. Mir bursts into happy tears and pretends it's soot.|It works. It works! They kiss you on the cheek and immediately start on version two.}
opt.left.say.1 [ce72f0] = {~它绕着工坊唱着你的名字，稍微有点走调，然后落在你手里。米尔喜极而泣，假装是被煤灰熏的。|成功了。成功了！TA 亲了一下你的脸颊，立刻开始做第二版。}
# en: {~It sings for three seconds and then explodes, gently, into springs. Mir is mortified. You laugh until they do too, and help them pick up every piece.|It sets your sleeve on fire. Mir has the bucket ready. "Version two," they say grimly.}
opt.left.say.2 [86dc39] = {~它唱了三秒，然后轻轻地炸成了一堆弹簧。米尔羞愧极了。你笑到 TA 也笑了，然后帮 TA 把每一个零件捡起来。|它把你的袖子点着了。米尔的水桶早就备好了。“第二版，”TA 阴沉地说。}
# en: Ask them how it works first
opt.right.label [0e03e7] = 先问 TA 它是怎么工作的
# en: {~They explain for an hour, with diagrams. You understand a third of it and love all of it. You wind it up together, very carefully, and it works.|Two hours of explanation and three cups of tea. The bird sings at the end. You've never been so proud of a thing you didn't make.}
opt.right.say.1 [8a2724] = {~TA 配着图解讲了一个小时。你听懂了三分之一，却爱上了全部。你们一起小心翼翼地上好发条，它成功了。|两个小时的讲解，三杯茶。最后那只鸟唱起了歌。你从没为一件不是自己做的东西这么骄傲过。}

@event kael_date_snow
# en: Snow, Just for You
title [63bfb8] = 只为你下的雪
# en: {Kael leads you to a corner of the lawn and makes it snow, only there, only on the two of you.|Another private snowfall. He's getting better at the shapes.|Kael has made it snow again. This time the flakes are stars.} {season == "summer": It's a hot day; the snow steams as it falls.|{~The flakes are as big as coins.|Somewhere a bird is very confused.|It's the most he's said with his hands in weeks.}}
text [098849] = {凯尔领你走到草坪的一角，让雪落下来，只落在那里，只落在你们两个身上。|又一场私人的雪。他造的形状越来越好了。|凯尔又下雪了。这一次雪花是星星的形状。} {season == "summer": 天很热；雪一边落一边冒着热气。|{~雪片大得像硬币。|某处有只鸟非常困惑。|这是他几个星期以来用双手说过最多的话。}}
# en: Snow falling over one small patch of a spring lawn, two students standing in it, one holding out his hand to catch the flakes.
scene [102324] = 雪落在春日草坪的一小块地方，两个学生站在其中，一个伸出手去接雪花。
# en: Catch the flakes
opt.left.label [0ecdf3] = 接雪花
# en: {~You catch them on your tongue and laugh, and Kael, astonishingly, laughs too, out loud. The snow falls harder when he's happy, it turns out.|You're both soaked and frozen. He warms your hands in his, which are, for the first time, warm.}
opt.left.say.1 [b7489f] = {~你用舌头接雪花，笑了起来，而凯尔，令人惊讶地，也笑出了声。原来他开心的时候，雪会下得更大。|你们俩都湿透了，冻僵了。他用双手焐着你的手，那双手第一次是暖的。}
# en: Ask him what it costs
opt.right.label [649ee9] = 问他这要付出什么
# en: {~"Nothing," he says. Then, honestly: "A little cold in the chest, for a day." You make him stop. He looks at you as if no one had ever asked him to.|He tells you about Northern frost-craft and what it takes. Then he makes one last snowflake, small, and lets you keep it.}
opt.right.say.1 [1701f0] = {~“什么都不用，”他说。然后，老实地：“胸口会冷上一天。”你让他停下。他看着你，好像从来没人这样要求过他。|他给你讲了北方的霜术，以及它需要付出什么。然后他造了最后一片雪花，小小的，让你留着。}

@event nessa_date_off_record
# en: Off the Record
title [a5d3b6] = 不留记录
# en: {Nessa locks the Ledger office, puts her quill in a drawer and says, "Off the record. All night."|Another night off the record. The quill sulks in its drawer.|Nessa has started saying "off the record" when she means "I love you". You've noticed.} {~There's a pot of tea and a plate of toast.|The proofs are stacked and, for once, ignored.|It's raining on the skylight.}
text [c549f0] = {内莎锁上《流明纪事报》编辑部的门，把羽毛笔放进抽屉，说：“不留记录。整晚。”|又一个不留记录的夜晚。羽毛笔在抽屉里生闷气。|内莎开始在想说“我爱你”的时候说“不留记录”了。你注意到了。} {~有一壶茶和一盘吐司。|校样摞得整整齐齐，难得一次被冷落在一边。|雨落在天窗上。}
# en: A newspaper office late at night, an enchanted quill lying still on a desk for once, two students sharing a pot of tea among the proofs.
scene [c29441] = 深夜的报社编辑部，一支施了魔法的羽毛笔难得安静地躺在桌上，两个学生在校样堆里分享一壶茶。
# en: Ask her about herself
opt.left.label [a87cd5] = 问她自己的事
# en: {~She talks about her childhood for an hour, which she never does: a printing shop, a father who read the news aloud. You don't take a single note. She notices.|Nessa, off the record, is quieter and funnier. You stay until the lamp runs out.}
opt.left.say.1 [15a3eb] = {~她讲了一个小时自己的童年，这是她从来不做的事：一家印刷铺，一个会把新闻大声读出来的父亲。你一个字的笔记都没记。她注意到了。|不留记录的内莎更安静，也更有趣。你一直待到灯油耗尽。}
# en: Tell her a secret of your own
opt.right.label [06d39a] = 告诉她一个你自己的秘密
# en: {~You tell her something nobody knows. She holds it like it's the most valuable story she's ever had, and never writes it down.|She listens, and then tells you one back. Off the record. It feels like a promise.}
opt.right.say.1 [8a6f7a] = {~你告诉了她一件没人知道的事。她像捧着自己得到过的最珍贵的故事那样捧着它，从没写下来。|她听完，也告诉了你一个。不留记录。这感觉像一个承诺。}
